{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.letter_multiplicative_iff_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.letter_multiplicative_iff_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.lean#L148-L167","doc":"An affine letter `c·σ + d·1` with `c ≠ 0` is right-multiplicative with\nscalar `φ` iff `σ` is, with scalar `(φ − d)/c`. So the interface letters of the\natom word (`pp`: `σ`, `nn`: `σ − h`, `pn`: `σ − h(½ − δ/4)`) inherit the\nobstruction above verbatim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.twoRow_not_rightLetterMultiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.twoRow_not_rightLetterMultiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.lean#L131-L146","doc":"Natural multiplicities, characteristic zero: a block in which `σ` has the\neigenvalue `q` with multiplicity `d₊ ≥ 1` and `−q⁻¹` with multiplicity `d₋ ≥ 1`\nis not letter-multiplicative. For `λ = (n−k, k)` two-row with `k ≥ 1`,\n`n − k ≥ 2`, both multiplicities are positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.mixedSpectrum_not_rightLetterMultiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.mixedSpectrum_not_rightLetterMultiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.lean#L104-L129","doc":"**Mixed spectrum excludes letter-multiplicativity.** If `χ(1) = d₊ + d₋`\nand `χ(σ) = d₊ q − d₋ q⁻¹` with both multiplicities non-zero (the trace of a\nrepresentation in which `σ` has both eigenvalues `q` and `−q⁻¹`), then no\nscalar `q'` makes `χ(x σ) = q' χ(x)` for all `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.root_of_rightLetterMultiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.root_of_rightLetterMultiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.lean#L87-L102","doc":"With `χ(1) ≠ 0` the scalar is one of the two Hecke eigenvalues. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.quadratic_of_rightLetterMultiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.quadratic_of_rightLetterMultiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.lean#L75-L85","doc":"Right-multiplicativity forces the scalar onto the Hecke quadratic:\n`(q'² − (q − q⁻¹) q' − 1) · χ(1) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.RightLetterMultiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.RightLetterMultiplicative","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.lean#L69-L73","doc":"`χ` is right-multiplicative for the letter `σ` with scalar `q'`:\n`χ(x σ) = q' χ(x)` for every `x`. This is what makes a letter contribute a\nfixed factor to the character of any word it is appended to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.HeckeRel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.HeckeRel","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MixedSpectrumCharacterNotLetterMultiplicative.lean#L65-L67","doc":"The Hecke relation for a generator `σ` with parameter `q`:\n`σ² = (q − q⁻¹) σ + 1` (the convention `(σ − q)(σ + q⁻¹) = 0` of §7a). ","signatureChunk":0}]}